00:01:02.109 --> 00:01:06.599
The question is to solve if the letters are distinct whole numbers from one to nine

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:14.549
the problem is AAA plus BBB plus CCC equals BAAC

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:18.989
I want to thank Luuk for sending me this email

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:27.749
Can you figure it out? Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for the solution

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:38.179
So how can we solve this addition problem?

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:46.609
Problems of this type usually involve some guessing and checking, so let's try to limit the possibilities to check

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.409
The first thing we can do is imagine we have the largest possible values for A B and C

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:59.180
This would be 999 + 888 + 777

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:04.020
This results in a sum of 2664

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:11.140
This is the largest possible value for BAAC. What does that mean?

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:14.020
Since it's less than 3000 and

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:21.260
since B is not equal to 0, that means there are only two possible values for the digit B

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:26.580
We could either have B = 2 or B = 1

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:34.960
So now let's further limit the number of possibilities using what we've just figured out

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:41.480
We have two cases where B is either equal to 1 or B is equal to 2

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.320
Now let's consider the sum in the unit's column

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.080
Notice we have A + 1 + C = C

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:57.320
In other words A + 1 + C = C + 10

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:03.530
If we cancel out the C we have that A + 1 = 10

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:06.679
This means that A = 9

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:14.080
Similarly in our other case we must have A + 2 + C = C,

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:20.820
which means A + 2 = 10 and therefore A = 8 in this case

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:31.540
So we either have 999 + 111 or 888 + 222

00:03:32.760 --> 00:03:42.460
So how can we figure out the value of C? Well remember that the largest possible sum was 2664

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.820
if we have A = 8 and B = 2

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:52.220
We end up with the sum that's larger than 2800

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:57.240
But this is larger than the largest possible sum we could have

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:05.520
Therefore we cannot have A = 8 and B = 2, so we can exclude this possibility

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:13.499
So we now know that A has to equal 9 and B has to equal 1, if there are any solutions

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.820
So is there any value of C that can make this possible?

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:27.329
Well let's add up what we know we have 999 + 111 which equals 1110

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.240
the final answer is 199C

00:04:32.860 --> 00:04:35.040
so if we take 199C

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:38.140
minus 1110

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:41.480
we end up with 88C

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:45.500
So that the total reaches

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:51.900
1990 C by adding CCC, we must have C = 8

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:54.960
So we put that in and

00:04:55.479 --> 00:04:57.479
we end up with something that works

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:59.560
This is our answer

00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:04.460
We have 999 plus 111 plus 888 equals

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:06.960
1998

